                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "073b8907-c98f-451b-8fdc-a87e75a3cd9a",
                        "entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "кри́тике"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "daa96a9f-0f4d-4cae-b04b-b9938417855b",
                        "entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "кри́тиках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ebdbd24-6888-3895-a5d6-06fcee077016",
                        "entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто критикует, выявляет недостатки, подвергает разбору, оценке что-либо, кого-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c9540a7-7886-4f67-881e-ddd235ad5d4a",
                                "sense_id": "7ebdbd24-6888-3895-a5d6-06fcee077016",
                                "text": "Казалось бы, ― ярый критик деятельности военного министерства, попавший, наконец, в его руководители, ― Гучков должен был показать, что необходимо сделать на посту военного министра для славы Родины."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3d49557-9f74-32fc-92f4-c1e64de29320",
                        "entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто профессионально занимается литературной, музыкальной, театральной и прочей критикой"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "622d26c9-415a-4048-9be7-4e92b0145104",
                                "sense_id": "d3d49557-9f74-32fc-92f4-c1e64de29320",
                                "text": "Впрочем, печатать я ему её не советую, потому что, к сожалению, в нынешних критиках я очень мало вкуса замечаю."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c724b67-15e8-4617-ad6b-1aca42cbb3be",
                                "sense_id": "d3d49557-9f74-32fc-92f4-c1e64de29320",
                                "text": "Кольцов целые месяцы жил со знаменитым критиком и вёл с ним обширную переписку; он был очень откровенен с Белинским, поверял ему многие самые интимные факты своей жизни."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd31645e-d1ad-4006-ae6e-2eff10eb27b7",
                                "sense_id": "d3d49557-9f74-32fc-92f4-c1e64de29320",
                                "text": "Дайте мне их книги, дайте мне их учения, их мемуары, и я, не будучи литературным критиком, берусь написать вам убедительнейшую литературную критику, в которой докажу ясно как день, что каждая страница их книг, брошюр, мемуаров написана прежде всего прежним русским помещиком."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9a4e6725-3a30-41aa-965b-04a452af19c5",
                        "source_entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "critic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "critic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f26c421e-65fb-375a-b8ea-31c7ea1fd7e0",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who appraises the works of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45c190dc-b515-4540-99e5-6a70612abd9c",
                                                "sense_id": "f26c421e-65fb-375a-b8ea-31c7ea1fd7e0",
                                                "text": "Following its publication, the novel received widespread acclaim from literary critics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3543f8d-5c4f-4545-804d-9b640526baa0",
                                                "sense_id": "f26c421e-65fb-375a-b8ea-31c7ea1fd7e0",
                                                "text": "The opinion of the most skilful critics was, that nothing finer [than Goldsmith's Traveller] had appeared in verse since the fourth book of the Dunciad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c95f868-70cf-384b-8b5d-0de3cab8ae31",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A specialist in judging works of art."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a6141c8-8569-35a0-ab53-76c5fd4293b4",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who criticizes; a person who finds fault."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df6a32e6-16c2-4fbe-af94-2edb782f9d1f",
                                                "sense_id": "1a6141c8-8569-35a0-ab53-76c5fd4293b4",
                                                "text": "When an author has many beauties consistent with virtue, piety, and truth, let not little critics exalt themselves, and shower down their ill nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33ca416b-ea96-3248-a734-66d6c648ceed",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An opponent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60ce05a1-535d-3ef2-b874-be6b7dc0d37b",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obsolete form of critique (“an act of criticism”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cf6e0ba-08dd-4533-868e-87c1cb7e6c6a",
                                                "sense_id": "60ce05a1-535d-3ef2-b874-be6b7dc0d37b",
                                                "text": "Make each day a Critick on the last."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3b15257-5f91-32d2-a607-792cbc75fa00",
                                        "entry_id": "418bfa4d-4caa-3823-8cc5-5f81b76c49a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obsolete form of critique (“the art of criticism”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b690dd2-3401-4864-80e1-b0cecf44c07b",
                                                "sense_id": "a3b15257-5f91-32d2-a607-792cbc75fa00",
                                                "text": "And, perhaps, if they were distinctly weighed, and duly considered, they would afford us another sort of logic and critic, than what we have been hitherto acquainted with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "critic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f7c5177-4c99-341a-b3bd-e36865bc7cf2",
                                        "entry_id": "595f2ee7-32b0-3c6a-97db-137d7a0ef025",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To criticise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "496b37d0-8f06-4dac-a589-fb92bcab73ed",
                                                "sense_id": "2f7c5177-4c99-341a-b3bd-e36865bc7cf2",
                                                "text": "1607, Antony Brewer (attributed), Lingua, or the Combat of the Five Senses for Superiority\nNay, if you begin to critic once, we shall never have done."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6d59f3a-b45a-46b4-8389-36a9a7c493c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "fab14f30-7f8a-3190-a2f3-12cf1446b4e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "anatomist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anatomist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2f58d9c-a2f9-3c28-a0b5-ebcffeb0a8d6",
                                        "entry_id": "5077b020-c864-324b-aa02-4179954042c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who studies, teaches, writes on, or does research on anatomy and anatomical structures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68b991f6-2b20-4964-b85a-a762db97dec2",
                                                "sense_id": "c2f58d9c-a2f9-3c28-a0b5-ebcffeb0a8d6",
                                                "text": "But we can no longer regard the mere fact of these diffuse condensations of the lung becoming yellow and caseous as an evidence of their tuberculous nature, especially since the pathological anatomists, and among them Virchow, have shown that formations of the most different kind, having not the slightest connection with tubercule— as, for example, old cancerous masses, lymphatic glands swollen by a hyperplasia of cells, hæmorrhagical infarctions, abscesses, &c.— undergo exactly the same caseous transformation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bc809de-c4b5-4d96-b9b6-b8bbed199a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "c2f58d9c-a2f9-3c28-a0b5-ebcffeb0a8d6",
                                                "text": "A plant anatomist receiving such samples can remove pickled wood and bark for anatomical study, then dry the remaining portions for inclusion in a xylarium."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fedf1d4-714f-4528-8df6-8e09338ccb8d",
                                                "sense_id": "c2f58d9c-a2f9-3c28-a0b5-ebcffeb0a8d6",
                                                "text": "Gall's science of “bump reading” would ultimately be abandoned as much for its fixation on social categories as for an inability within the scientific community to replicate its findings. These scientific failings would be exposed by anatomists like Paul Broca (1861) and Carl Wernicke (1874) who pioneered the alternative neuroscientific method of lesion–symptom mapping."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
